.\"	$GergiOS: auditctl.8,v 1.0 2026/07/10 $
.\"
.Dd July 10, 2026
.Dt AUDITCTL 8
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm auditctl
.Nd control the audit daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl s
.Nm
.Fl e
.Cm enable | disable
.Nm
.Fl f
.Nm
.Fl r
.Nm
.Fl R
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command controls the audit daemon
.Xr auditd 8 .
It communicates with
.Nm auditd
via IPC and allows the administrator to check status and
perform management actions.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s
Show audit daemon status including whether logging is enabled,
whether the log file is open, and the poll interval.
.It Fl e Cm enable | disable
Enable or disable audit logging.
When disabled, auditd stops polling the kernel audit buffer
until it is re-enabled.
.It Fl f
Force an immediate poll of the kernel audit buffer.
All pending audit records are flushed to the log file.
.It Fl r
Reopen the audit log file.
This is useful when an external tool rotates the log.
.It Fl R
Force log rotation.
auditd will rename the current log with a timestamp, open a new
log file, and clean up old rotated logs according to the retention
policy in
.Xr auditd.conf 5 .
.It Fl h
Show usage summary.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/log/audit/audit.log -compact
.It Pa /etc/auditd.conf
Audit daemon configuration file.
.It Pa /var/log/audit/audit.log
Default audit log file.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr auditd 8 ,
.Xr auditd.conf 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in GergiOS 1.0.
